                <pb facs="0886" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/1578: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-31T16:00:00-05:00">March 31, 1933—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Your 54, March 29, 4 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d732-f1"/> You may inform the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>That the Convention for renewal of the General Claims
                                Commission<anchor n="3" xml:id="d732-f2"/> does not require prior
                            advice and consent to ratification by the Senate of the United States
                            and may be brought into force at any time by exchange of
                            ratifications.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>That inasmuch as the protocol supplementing the Convention for renewal
                            of the Special Claims Commission<anchor n="4" xml:id="d732-f3"/>
                            contains subject matter deemed to be not within the purview of the
                            original Convention of September 10, 1923,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d732-f4"
                            /> that Convention has been submitted to the Senate of the United States
                            for its advice and consent to ratification. The matter has been referred
                            to the Senate Committee on Foreign Relations and is still
                            pending.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
